8 hanging to the rook on a1. That's a whole rook on offer."},{"title":"What it does instead","text":"It takes the knight on b5."},{"title":"If White takes the rook","text":"10.Rxa8 is met by 10…Bb7, threatening …Bxa8, winning a rook. Then 11…h6 threatens …hxg5, winning a bishop, and 13…Nxe4 takes the e4 pawn. Black is a pawn down: Black is a little better (−0.54). This is White's best try."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 9…Qb6, is clearly weaker (+1.19 against −0.54). White answers 10.Nc3. That would leave Black a little worse."}]},{"ply":34,"name":"17…g5","cls":"mistake","color":"b","headline":"17…g5 is a mistake: Black's winning chances go from 44% to 30%.","points":["White answers 18.Bg3, which brings the bishop, White's least active piece, into play (from 1 to 4 usable squares).","Moves a pawn from in front of the king, loosening its cover.","Better was 17…Nb6 (+0.67): moving away uncovers the queen on d8, which now hits the d4 pawn."],"better":"17…Nb6 prepares …Qd5 and opens the line of the queen on d8 to the d4 pawn. After 18.Rfd1 Qd5 19.Ne1 c2 20.Rdc1 Qxd4 21.Ra2, Black comes out a pawn up (+0.67)."},{"ply":35,"name":"18.Bg3","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"18.Bg3! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Moves the attacked bishop to safety.","Brings the bishop, White's least active piece, into play (from 1 to 4 usable squares).","The next best move, 18.Ne5, would drop White's winning chances from 70% to 52% (+0.26).","18.Bg3 gets the bishop out of the way of …gxh4.","Black was threatening …gxh4, winning a bishop for a pawn. The bishop steps away.","Black answers 18…Nb6, opening the line of the queen on d8 to the d4 pawn."]},{"ply":50,"name":"25…Rb8","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"25…Rb8 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 37% to 16%.","points":["White answers 26.Nxg4, which takes the pawn on g4.","After Nxg4, White wins 1 point of material within 4 moves.","Better was 25…Bxe5 (+1.48), which takes the knight on e5."],"better":"25…Bxe5 stops Nxg4. Engine line: 26.dxe5 Bf3 27.Qc4 Ne4 28.Bc6 Rd8 (+1.48)."}],"opening":{"name":"Queen's Gambit Declined: Traditional Variation","eco":"D30","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 7.Nc3: 13 moves in all, 7 by White and 6 by Black.","Black left the book with 7…a6. In 75 games from this position, strong players played 7…Qb6 (39%), 7…Bb4 (31%), 7…b4 (20%) or 7…h6 (4%).","The main line goes on 7…Qb6 8.Be2.","From here White scored 56% in those games, with 13% drawn."]}}